<title>USA: Pharmaceutical Marketing Q2 oper shr $0.11.</title>
<headline>Pharmaceutical Marketing Q2 oper shr $0.11.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>PHARMACEUTICAL MARKETING SERVICES INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>				(in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended   Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				   December 31,	  December 31,</p>
<p>				   1996	1995	1996	1995</p>
<p> Revenue		     $26,552  $24,290    $48,474  $44,999</p>
<p>Income from continuing</p>
<p>  operations		   1,457    2,380	1,683    2,498</p>
<p>Loss from discontinued</p>
<p>  operations		 (9,914)  (1,081)    (9,914)  (1,754)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	  (8,457    1,299    (8,231)	744</p>
<p>Income (loss) per share:</p>
<p>    Continuing operations   0.11     0.18	 0.13     0.19</p>
<p>Discontinued operations,</p>
<p>	net		     (0.74)   (0.08)     (0.74)   (0.13)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per share</p>
<p>				  (0.63)     0.10     (0.61)     0.06</p>
<p>Common stock and common stock</p>
<p>   equivalents		13,328   13,404     13,248   13,337</p>
<p>NOTE: The results for the second quarter of fiscal 1996 included certain non-recurring gains. If these items were to be excluded, net income in the second quarter of 1997 would be $0.2 million higher than for the same quarter in 1996.</p>
<p>Currency exchange impacts reduced revenue for the half year by $1.9 million. Income from continuing operations was $1.7 million, or $0.13 per share, compared with $2.5 million, or $0.19 per share, in the previous period. The decrease in operating income is a result of the non-recurring items in the second quarter of fiscal 1996.</p>
